  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Salām – the word that opens every door",
   "md": "[[سلام|salām|hello]] literally means *peace*. Iranians say it to everyone – the taxi driver, the shopkeeper, a child, a stranger on the stairs – and it works at any hour. If you learn one word today, learn this one.\n\nYou will also hear [[مرسی|mersi|thanks]] (from French) and [[ممنون|mamnun|grateful]] everywhere; both mean *thanks*. The fuller [[متشکرم|motshakker-am|I thank you]] is a little more formal.\n\nPersian has two words for *you*: [[تو|to|you (one person, informal)]] and [[شما|shomā|you (plural, or one person politely)]]. With anyone you do not know well, use **shomā** – it is the safe, respectful choice, like French *vous*. Friends and family use **to**."
  },
